course: dictionary
lesson: 3280
title: Es: a word from other languages
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Es» is not an English word, so you will not find it in an English sentence about your day. You will meet it in other languages and in science, and it is worth knowing what it means there.
explain: In Spanish, «es» means «is». «Es grande» means «it is big», so es is a form of the verb «to be», just like is.
explain: In French, «Tu es blessé ?» means «Are you hurt?». Blessé means hurt, and the s in es is silent, so it sounds like «eh». Use the words around it to check: a question about being hurt fits the word blessé.
explain: English has its own ending, -es. It makes some plurals (box, boxes; bus, buses) and some he/she verbs (she watches, he goes).
fact: «Es» is not an English word, but it is used in Spanish and French.
fact: In Spanish, «¿Qué es?» means «what is it?».
fact: In French, «blessé» means hurt, and «une blessure» is an injury.
fact: In English, add -es after s, ss, sh, ch, x and z, as in buses, kisses, wishes, watches, boxes and buzzes.
fact: «Es» is also the chemical symbol for einsteinium, an element made in laboratories.
exercise: «Tu es blessé ?» means what in English? | Are you tired? | *Are you hurt? | Are you ready to go? | Is it blue?
exercise: «Es grande» means what in Spanish? | You are big | *It is big | It is small | Where is it?
exercise: Which word takes -es to make its plural? | cat | dog | *box | tree
test: In Spanish, «¿Qué es?» means what? | How old are you? | Who is he? | *What is it? | Where are you?
test: Which sentence uses the -es ending for he or she? | *She watches the film. | They walk to school. | I walk to school. | We walk to school.
exam: In French, «Tu es» means what in English? | I am | *You are | They are | We are
